.TH "ODIR-RERUN" "7" "" "odir 25.1.2+onesimus.0.2.0" "Onesimus Director Commands"
.SH NAME
odir\-rerun \- rerun: Rerun a job
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
rerun [jobid=<jobid>[,...]] [since_jobid=<since_jobid>] [until_jobid=<until_jobid>] [days=<days>] [hours=<hours>] [yes]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Starts earlier jobs again with the parameters they ran with (job, level, client, fileset, pool). Jobs are chosen by JobId, by a JobId range with since_jobid= and until_jobid=, or by a time window with days= and hours=. For every job the Director shows the run summary and asks yes, mod or no; yes on the command line starts all chosen jobs without asking.
.PP
since_jobid=, days= and hours= consider only jobs that ended with a fatal error (status f); for days= and hours= the scheduled start time counts, and both values add up. until_jobid= is only valid together with since_jobid=. Before rerunning several jobs found this way the Director lists the JobIds and asks for confirmation.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.SS "rerun"
.TP
.B "jobid=<jobid>[,...]"
Job ID (text; several values separated by commas)
.TP
.B "since_jobid=<since_jobid>"
Rerun failed jobs since this JobId (number)
.TP
.B "until_jobid=<until_jobid>"
Up to this JobId (number)
.TP
.B "days=<days>"
Failed jobs of the last days (number)
.TP
.B "hours=<hours>"
Failed jobs of the last hours (number)
.TP
.B "yes"
Do not ask (keyword)
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B "rerun jobid=42"
run job 42 again with its original parameters
.TP
.B "rerun days=1 yes"
restart every job that failed during the last day
.TP
.B "rerun since_jobid=100 until_jobid=120"
failed jobs between JobId 100 and 120
.SH ORIGIN
Bareos console command.
